        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3(x+6)=28$, so $x=3\\frac{1}{3}$.",
          "worked": "Let $x$ be the number.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3(x+6)&=28\\\\3x+18&=28\\\\3x&=10\\\\x&=\\frac{10}{3}\\\\x&=3\\frac{1}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: $3\\left(\\frac{10}{3}+6\\right)=3\\times\\frac{28}{3}=28$.",
